Subject: Utils: add globalShortcutTexts(), every chord bound to a global action

globalShortcutText() returns the first multi-key sequence of an action, in
the order kglobalaccel hands them back, which is not stable between
sessions; a page that wants to name one particular chord of several cannot
choose it. globalShortcutTexts() returns all of them, as native text.

--- a/src/public/utils.cpp
+++ b/src/public/utils.cpp
@@ -115,6 +115,20 @@
     return shortcuts.first().toString(QKeySequence::NativeText);
 }
 
+QStringList Utils::globalShortcutTexts(const QString &componentName, const QString &actionId) const
+{
+    // Every sequence bound to the action, in kglobalaccel's order, so a page
+    // can pick the one it wants to teach instead of whichever comes first.
+    QStringList texts;
+    const auto shortcuts = KGlobalAccel::self()->globalShortcut(componentName, actionId);
+    for (const QKeySequence &shortcut : shortcuts) {
+        if (!shortcut.isEmpty()) {
+            texts.append(shortcut.toString(QKeySequence::NativeText));
+        }
+    }
+    return texts;
+}
